1. General criteria
(a) The aggravated fine criteria based on the number of violations apply where an administrative fine has been imposed for the same violation during the last three years. The period shall be calculated by reference to the date on which an administrative fine was imposed for the violation and the date on which the same violation was detected again after that disposition.
(b) Where an aggravated disposition is imposed under item (a), the applicable violation level shall be the next level after that of the disposition preceding the violation (where two or more administrative fine dispositions were imposed within the period under item (a), the highest level shall apply).
(c) The imposing authority may reduce the fine amount under the individual criteria in subparagraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases: Provided, That this shall not apply to a violator who is in arrears with administrative fines.
1) Where the violation is recognized as resulting from negligence, such as minor carelessness or error;
2) Where the violator has corrected or eliminated the consequences of the unlawful act;
3) Where reduction of the fine amount is otherwise deemed necessary in consideration of the degree of the violation, its motive and consequences, etc.
(d) The imposing authority may increase the fine amount under the individual criteria in subparagraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases: Provided, That even an increased fine shall not exceed the maximum amount under Article 65 (1) and (2) of the Act.
1) Where the nature and degree of the violation are serious and the damage to users is deemed substantial;
2) Where the state of violation of the Act has continued for at least two months;
3) Where an increase in the fine amount is otherwise deemed necessary in consideration of the degree of the violation, its motive and consequences, etc.

